  "post_stream": {
    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 6141,
        "name": "BaloTheJester",
        "username": "BaloTheJester",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/balothejester/{size}/2080_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-08T19:00:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi all,</p>\n<p>I couldn’t find a clear statement about this in the rulebook, and it only seems to apply in one or two weird corner cases, but I wanted to double-check: If a hero is defeated while they are producing some sort of ongoing (not necessarily Ongoing) effect, when does that effect end?</p>\n<p>Example: Ra, Mr. Fixer, Haka, and Legacy (turns taken in that order) are all fighting Grand Warlord Voss. Legacy has only 1 HP remaining.</p>\n<p>On Legacy’s turn, he uses Galvanize during his Power Phase.</p>\n<p>The environment turn passes without any damage being dealt, then on Voss’s turn, he does 2 damage to the hero with the lowest HP, thus defeating Legacy.</p>\n<p>All of Legacy’s cards immediately get destroyed, and his Character Card gets flipped.  But, do Ra, Mr. Fixer, and Haka all get to do +1 damage on their turns from the Galvanize, or does Legacy’s Galvanize fade as soon as he’s defeated?</p>\n<p>I’m unclear on what should happen here. Legacy’s Character Card did not go out of play, and this is one of a very, very few cards that have a persistent effect that would at all logically persist beyond the life of the card. (I actually can’t think of any others, but want to cover all angles).</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:35:59.628Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
