      {
        "id": 36085,
        "name": "awp832",
        "username": "awp832",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/a9a28c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-08T19:14:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>It depends.   If it is a card that is in play, such as Inspiring Presence, the card is destroyed and its effects canceled.</p>\n<p>However, in the case of Galvanize, which is something that lasts until Legacy’s next turn,  or otherwise isn’t reliant on a card actually being in play…   the effects would be maintained.   Heroic Interception works the same way currently, as does Take Down.  although I believe those are set to be changed in the Enhanced Edition.   Other cards that could work this way are Hypersonic Assault, Ground Pound, and Adhesive Foam Grenade.</p>\n<p>Legacy still gets his turn,   he’s not out of the game,  its just that his options are much more limited.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:09:57.640Z",
